<% if dossier.dig('teleprompter_script', 'act_1') %><%= dossier.dig('teleprompter_script', 'act_1').strip %><% if act1_story && !dossier.dig('teleprompter_script', 'act_1').include?(act1_story['story'].to_s) %> [PERSONAL RECOLLECTION: <%= act1_story['story'] %>]<% end %><% elsif dossier['episode'] == 0 %>Welcome to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall, and this is our preparatory pilot. In October 2026, I walked out underneath 345,000-volt transmission lines in Northern Illinois with a smartphone to record a field dispatch on software craftsmanship and identity. When I checked the footage back at my desk, the audio sounded completely destroyed: deafening 60 Hz electromagnetic hum, corona arcing, and an apparent three-and-a-half-minute clock drift. Trashing the footage and reshooting is the standard advice. But working through that recording became a living case study in what happens when we lean on modern AI models, and why the bottleneck in engineering is never generation: it is verification.<% if act1_story %> [PERSONAL RECOLLECTION: <%= act1_story['story'] %>]<% end %><% else %>Welcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter <%= dossier['era_name'] %>. Before automated code synthesis and agent workflows, developers met face to face to establish standards of craftsmanship. Today we rewatch Episode <%= dossier['episode'] %>: <%= dossier['interviewee'] %> from <%= dossier['conference'] %>.<% if act1_story %> [PERSONAL RECOLLECTION: <%= act1_story['story'] %>]<% end %><% end %>
